cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the information below."

title: "KG-Eval: Knowledge Graph-Based Benchmark Evaluation Toolkit"

version: 0.1.0

date-released: 2026-05-26

url: "https://github.com/sanchari1992/kg_eval"

repository-code: "https://github.com/sanchari1992/kg_eval"

license: MIT

abstract: >
  KG-Eval is a lightweight Python toolkit for constructing knowledge graphs
  from text datasets and evaluating large language model outputs using
  structural, semantic, reasoning, and linguistic complexity metrics.
  It supports hallucination analysis across multiple biomedical QA benchmarks
  including PubMedQA and BioASQ.

keywords:
  - knowledge graphs
  - hallucination detection
  - large language models
  - biomedical NLP
  - benchmark evaluation
  - graph-based metrics

